WEBVTT

00:00.780 --> 00:04.750
Now we have a very, very,
very hairy expression.

00:04.750 --> 00:09.375
And once again, I'm going to
see if you can simplify this.

00:09.375 --> 00:11.000
And I'll give you
little time to do it.

00:13.680 --> 00:17.480
So this one is even crazier than
the last few we've looked at.

00:17.480 --> 00:20.960
We've got y's and
xy's, and x squared

00:20.960 --> 00:25.730
and x's, well more just xy's and
y squared and on and on and on.

00:25.730 --> 00:28.370
And there will be a temptation,
because you see a y here

00:28.370 --> 00:29.940
and a y here to
say, oh, maybe I can

00:29.940 --> 00:32.549
add this negative
3y plus this 4xy

00:32.549 --> 00:34.830
somehow since I see a y and a y.

00:34.830 --> 00:37.360
But the important
thing to realize here

00:37.360 --> 00:40.380
is that a y is
different than an xy.

00:40.380 --> 00:41.810
Think about it
they were numbers.

00:41.810 --> 00:46.672
If y was 3 and an x was a
2, then a y would be a 3

00:46.672 --> 00:49.270
while an xy would have been a 6.

00:49.270 --> 00:52.010
And a y is very different
than a y squared.

00:52.010 --> 00:54.710
Once again, if the why it
took on the value 3, then

00:54.710 --> 00:57.270
the y squared would
be the value 9.

00:57.270 --> 00:59.580
So even though you see
the same letter here,

00:59.580 --> 01:03.640
they aren't the same-- I
guess you cannot add these two

01:03.640 --> 01:05.480
or subtract these two terms.

01:05.480 --> 01:07.610
A y is different
than a y squared,

01:07.610 --> 01:09.860
is different than an xy.

01:09.860 --> 01:12.640
Now with that said, let's
see if there is anything

01:12.640 --> 01:14.480
that we can simplify.

01:14.480 --> 01:16.700
So first, let's think
about the y terms.

01:16.700 --> 01:18.060
So you have a negative 3y there.

01:18.060 --> 01:20.140
Do we have any more y term?

01:20.140 --> 01:20.710
Yes, we do.

01:20.710 --> 01:22.889
We have this 2y
right over there.

01:22.889 --> 01:24.930
So I'll just write it
out-- I'll just reorder it.

01:24.930 --> 01:28.860
So we have negative 3y plus 2y.

01:31.740 --> 01:33.770
Now, let's think
about-- and I'm just

01:33.770 --> 01:36.380
going in an arbitrary order,
but since our next term is an xy

01:36.380 --> 01:38.970
term-- let's think about
all of the xy terms.

01:38.970 --> 01:41.945
So we have plus 4xy
right over here.

01:41.945 --> 01:43.570
So let me just write
it down-- I'm just

01:43.570 --> 01:47.200
reordering the whole
expression-- plus 4xy.

01:47.200 --> 01:50.990
And then I have minus
4xy right over here.

01:54.710 --> 01:56.550
Then let's go to
the x squared terms.

01:56.550 --> 01:59.810
I have negative 2 times x
squared, or minus 2x squared.

01:59.810 --> 02:01.830
So let's look at this.

02:01.830 --> 02:04.590
So I have minus 2x squared.

02:04.590 --> 02:06.360
Do I have any other x squared?

02:06.360 --> 02:07.080
Yes, I do.

02:07.080 --> 02:09.240
I have this 3x squared
right over there.

02:09.240 --> 02:12.720
So plus 3x squared.

02:12.720 --> 02:17.990
And then let's see, I have
an x term right over here,

02:17.990 --> 02:20.220
and that actually looks
like the only x term.

02:20.220 --> 02:22.390
So that's plus 2x.

02:22.390 --> 02:24.190
And then I only
have one y squared

02:24.190 --> 02:29.320
term-- I'll circle that in
orange-- so plus y squared.

02:29.320 --> 02:31.880
So all I have done is I've
reordered the statement

02:31.880 --> 02:34.820
and I've color coded it based
on the type of term we have.

02:34.820 --> 02:37.160
And now it should be
a little bit simpler.

02:37.160 --> 02:38.740
So let's try it out.

02:38.740 --> 02:41.580
If I have negative
3 of something

02:41.580 --> 02:43.524
plus 2 of that something,
what do I have?

02:43.524 --> 02:45.690
Or another way to say it,
if I have two of something

02:45.690 --> 02:48.730
and I subtract 3 of that,
what am I left with?

02:48.730 --> 02:50.940
Well, I'm left with negative
1 of that something.

02:50.940 --> 02:55.872
So I could write negative 1y, or
I could just write negative y.

02:55.872 --> 02:57.580
And another way you
could think about it,

02:57.580 --> 02:59.496
but I like to think about
it intuitively more,

02:59.496 --> 03:00.960
is what's the coefficient here?

03:00.960 --> 03:02.254
It is negative 3.

03:02.254 --> 03:03.420
What's the coefficient here?

03:03.420 --> 03:04.160
It's 2.

03:04.160 --> 03:05.576
Where obviously
both are dealing--

03:05.576 --> 03:07.440
they're both y
terms, not xy terms,

03:07.440 --> 03:09.880
not y squared terms, just y.

03:09.880 --> 03:12.560
And so negative 3
plus 2 is negative 1,

03:12.560 --> 03:16.000
or negative 1y is the
same thing as negative y.

03:16.000 --> 03:19.300
So those simplify to
this right over here.

03:19.300 --> 03:21.180
Now let's look at the xy terms.

03:21.180 --> 03:24.560
If I have 4 of
this, 4 xy's and I

03:24.560 --> 03:29.060
were to take away 4 xy's,
how many xy's am I left with?

03:29.060 --> 03:30.890
Well, I'm left with no xy's.

03:30.890 --> 03:33.170
Or you could say add
the coefficients,

03:33.170 --> 03:36.740
4 plus negative 4,
gives you 0 xy's.

03:36.740 --> 03:39.450
Either way, these
two cancel out.

03:39.450 --> 03:41.120
If I have 4 of something
and I take away

03:41.120 --> 03:44.350
those 4 of that something,
I'm left with none of them.

03:44.350 --> 03:46.940
And so I'm left with no xy's.

03:46.940 --> 03:48.830
And then I have
right over here--

03:48.830 --> 03:51.910
I could have written
0xy, but that

03:51.910 --> 03:54.420
seems unnecessary--
then right over here

03:54.420 --> 03:56.160
I have my x squared terms.

03:56.160 --> 03:58.700
Negative 2 plus 3 is 1.

03:58.700 --> 04:01.240
Or another way of saying
it, if I have 3x squared

04:01.240 --> 04:02.830
and I were to take
away 2 of those x

04:02.830 --> 04:05.540
squared, so I'm left
with the 1x squared.

04:05.540 --> 04:09.140
So this right over here
simplifies to 1x squared.

04:09.140 --> 04:10.950
Or I could literally
just write x squared.

04:10.950 --> 04:13.450
1x squared is the same
thing as x squared.

04:13.450 --> 04:16.779
So plus x squared,
and then these there's

04:16.779 --> 04:18.260
nothing really left to simplify.

04:18.260 --> 04:23.675
So plus 2x plus y squared.

04:27.365 --> 04:27.990
And we're done.

04:27.990 --> 04:29.000
And obviously you
might have gotten

04:29.000 --> 04:31.250
an answer in some other
order, but the order

04:31.250 --> 04:33.059
in which I write these
terms don't matter.

04:33.059 --> 04:35.100
It just matters that you
were able to simplify it

04:35.100 --> 04:37.535
to these four terms.
